  Partly I disagree.  Unicorn horns are two-handed.  Which brings in the
problem of getting cursed.  It also prevents wearing a shield.  Even a
+0 dwarven or elven shield has a base AC of 2.  Unihorns also are range
1.  As a result of that any skill slots used on unihorns will be lost
after getting the Staff of Aesculapius.

  Partly I agree.  Unihorns don't have to be #enhanced to Expert.  At
basic they average 6.5 damage and have an intrinsic +1 to hit.  That's
fine right there as far as I'm concerned.  Another advantage is as a
backup weapon if the Wizard of Yendor steals the Staff.  Especially as
you'll be keeping unicorn horn throughout the game no matter what weapon
you're using (As you point out above).

  So 1 skill slot for unihorn.  6.5 average damage, +1 to hit, benefits
of applying a unihorn, backup weapon.  First downside is no shield. A
healer using the Staff has the same problem, but by the time a healer
can get a unihorn that may not be a problem.  Second downside is that
it's going to be a while before a healer gets a unicorn horn.  Maybe a
long time.


