  Maxing out dart and dagger looks redundant.  Getting dagger to skilled
gives d2 daggers per fling.  That's plenty.  The thing to remember is
that while Expert multishot is awesome, Skilled is still great.  Even
single shot missile weapons are pretty darn good.  

  The main point is to hit the monster with as many missiles as possible
before it reaches you.  It doesn't matter if it's d5 or 1 at a time.
With range up to 9 that's possible that's probably 5 missiles.  Not bad
at all.

>leaves 16 slots to divide among knife,
>quarterstaff and unihorn.  Bring all 3 up to Skilled
>costs 8 leaving 8 to spend.  Hold a couple for arriving
>artifacts and that tells me healers should go to Expert
>at either unihorn or knife but not both.  If I did the
>arthimatic right.

  It looks like the real lessson from all this is that Healers shouldn't
automatically max out their skills on any weapon.



  Check found quarterstaffs for enchantment.  (Assume quarterstaffs in
wizard bones are +1).  If you find an enchanted non-cursed quarterstaff
you're set.  For those avoiding decisions this looks like the way to go.
Take it to at least Skilled.  (Per your excellent recommendation above.)

  Use the Staff of Aesculapius and hope the RNG likes you.  Again, take
to Skilled.

  Unicorn horn - take to basic no matter what as a backup weapon if the
Staff gets stolen.

  That's just 3 skill slots.  Add in the 4 for Expert healing and it's
just 7.  Could easily be 6 by holding Healing at Skilled.  That leaves 8
spare skill slots by XL 14 to divide between darts, daggers, and
scalpel.

  Darts, I have reluctantly concluded, don't make sense.  Sure d3
blessed +7 poisoned darts with max luck are awesome.  You won't have any
of those early on when you really need them.  Which is not to say
they're not a good idea later if you want to level up to get the slots.
It's just that early on rocks or glass work almost as well.  Knives or
daggers will be even better because they won't disappear.  (A +0 dart
has a 2/3 chance of disappearing per hit.  That's just too horrible to
contemplate.)

  Yes, I know knives don't get multi-shot.  So what?  As I said before,
if you start throwing early enough the difference between multi- and
single-shot isn't as great.


  It looks like daggers or knives as both wielded weapon and missile
weapon.  Daggers are slightly better, but healers start with a scalpel
(knife skill).  Knifes also benefit crysknives.  But those will be
later, perhaps much later.  Crysknives also have the 'revert' problem.

  I'd say go with daggers.  d2 per fling at Skilled.  A neutral healer
(Is there any other kind?) may get Magicbane as a divine gift.  +2 to
hit when wielded or thrown.  (Knives only get +2 to hit when thrown.)

  If wizards can start Unskilled with no daggers and work up to Skilled
with a stack of daggers, so can healers.  Best of all thrown d2 daggers
can still be used after switching to unihorn, the Staff, or random
divine gift as the wielded weapon.  


  Which is not to say knives should be ignored.  Pick up any you find
and throw them until you get some daggers.  Use autoquiver so you'll
automatically throw knives after you run out of daggers.  Keep wielding
the scalpel until you get to basic in dagger.  Then switch to wielded
dagger to speed up #enhancing dagger skill.

  I'd say name your first non-cursed Elven dagger as Sting.  The orc
spotting is a big help against orc hordes.  Then name Orcrist when
possible to help chew up orc hordes maneuvered into a chokepoint based
on Sting's orc spotting.  (You're getting the Staff.  What do you care
about other artifacts?)


  So:  

  Dagger to Skilled asap:  3 slots.  Temporary wielded weapon. Permanent
ranged weapon even with the Staff or a unicorn horn.  Two for the price
of one.

  Healing spells to Skilled: 1 slot.  (Spell skills are different from
weapon skills in this regard.)

  Quarterstaff to skilled: 3 slots.  Wait until getting the Staff of
Aesculapius if you don't get an enchanted quarterstaff before then.

  Unihorn to basic: 1 slot as emergency backup even if not used as
primary weapon.  Cheap at the price.

  That's a total of 8 skill slots.  Enough left over to do darts to
Expert and unihorn to Skilled if you like (Based on XL:14 for the
Quest).  Or #enhance both Healing and Quarterstaff to Expert.


